<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Quickstart</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; margin: 3rem; color: #222; }
        .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
        .connected { background: #d7f3df; color: #14532d; }
        .plain { background: #fde8e8; color: #7a1f1f; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>It works.</h1>

    {% if runtimeConnected %}
        <p><span class="badge connected">runtime connected</span> — this window is the
        NativePHP Electron runtime, and this page came from <code>Bootstrapper::boot()</code>
        opening it.</p>
    {% else %}
        <p><span class="badge plain">plain browser</span> — the same route, the same
        controller, no runtime attached. A native app you cannot open in a browser is a
        native app you cannot develop.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <p>This is the smallest app the <a href="https://github.com/sadiqk2/nativephp-symfony">
    project README</a> describes: one config file, one bootstrapper, one route. See
    <a href="../demo/README.md">../demo</a> for a fuller example — both bundles, several
    screens, a native menu.</p>
</body>
</html>
